verification_parameters.description:
A string containing the viewability parameters to be sent along with impressions.

- For MOAT, it is an escaped JSON string.
  - Example: `{\"campaign_name\": \"{campaign_name}\", \"ad_group_name\": \"{ad_group_name}\"}`
- For DoubleVerify, it uses URL query string syntax.
  - Example: `campaign_name={campaign_name}&ad_group_name={ad_group_name}`

Both vendors accept the following macros:
  - {ad_account_name}
  - {campaign_name}
  - {ad_group_name}
  - {ad_name}

DoubleVerify also accepts the following macros:
  - {ad_account_id}
  - {campaign_id}
  - {ad_group_id}
  - {ad_id}

CustomAudiences.description:
Custom audiences to include or exclude for ad delivery.

It contains the custom audience IDs to include or exclude for ad delivery.

If it's empty, it will be delivered to all users.

* e.g. This will target all users
  ```
  {
    ...
    "custom_audiences": {
      "include": [],
      "exclude": []
    }
  }
  ```
* e.g. This will target users who are in custom audience `123`
  ```
  {
    "custom_audiences": {
        "include": [123],
        "exclude": []
      }
  }
  ```

all_ad_account_access.description:
Set to true to grant all DA ad accounts of the business access to this
catalog. Once enabled it cannot be reverted to specific ad accounts;
a request attempting to set it back to false is rejected with 400.
